# Line endings
#
# Without this file, a clone on Windows with the default `core.autocrlf=true`
# gets CRLF in the working tree while Biome formats to LF — so `biome check`
# failed on ~90 files that nobody had actually touched, and any contributor
# who ran `--write` produced a diff of pure line-ending noise.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises every text file to LF in the repository AND in
# the working tree, on every platform, regardless of each developer's
# core.autocrlf setting. That matches Biome's default, so formatting is
# reproducible everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.glb binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
*.task binary

# Generated — collapse in pull-request diffs.
bun.lock linguist-generated=true
*.lock linguist-generated=true
